The revised retention schedule is adopted and takes effect March 1. Drawing=
s, specifications and record documents are retained permanently. Project co=
rrespondence, meeting minutes, transmittals and submittal and ASI logs are =
retained for fifteen years from closeout. Contract and insurance documents =
follow the same fifteen year term. Accounting records follow the statutory =
seven.<br />
<br />
Two changes to how this is enforced. Projects closed within seven years now=
 sit in the nearline tier rather than deep, so retrieval is minutes and fre=
e. And a legal hold flag now exists at the project folder level. If a folde=
r carries the flag, the tiering and retention automation skips it entirely =
and nothing in it can be deleted by anyone, including me.<br />
<br />
Perpetua and Priscilla maintain the hold list and it is reviewed every quar=
ter.